title: The Doors Are Open
subtitle: Workers queue to join the party in one district.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('recruits'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('recruits');
Q.lw_n = RG.lw.rnd(3, 9) * 100;
RG.news(Q.lw_n + ' new members in one week in ' + Q.lw_town);
!}

= The Doors Are Open

The district office in **[+ lw_town +]** has run out of membership cards. In one week, [+ lw_n +] workers from [+ lw_works +] and the streets around it have asked to join, some with their union books in their hands, some with nothing but a cap. The district secretary has been writing names on the backs of leaflets.

It is the best news [+ lw_d_name +] has had in a year. It is also a problem: half the new members have never been to a meeting of any kind, and the other half have been to meetings of every kind.

- @open: Take them all, and put them to work at once.
- @school: Make them candidates first, with evening classes.
- @unions: Send them into the unions and the works councils.

@open
subtitle: The district grows fast and gets restless. Not every new member will stay, or listen. The Left's way.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.12, militancy: 4, loyalty: -5});
Q.unity -= 2;
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 3);
!}

The new members get their cards on Saturday and their first leaflets to hand out on Sunday. By the end of the month, the district holds meetings nobody planned and passes motions nobody drafted.

@school
subtitle: Slower growth, but solid. The district comes closer to the Zentrale. The Spartacist way.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.05, loyalty: 6});
Q.unity += 2;
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 4);
!}

Every candidate attends six evenings: the Communist Manifesto, the history of the German revolution, the statutes of the party, and how to speak at a meeting without being shouted down. Most of them come back for more.

@unions
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The new members become the party's voice in the works. The Right's line.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids working inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
RG.lw.against('union_work');
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: 0.06, loyalty: 2});
Q.worker_support += 2;
RG.lw.lean('unionist', 1, 4);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 0, -2);
!}

Each new member is told the same thing: keep your union book, go to every branch meeting, and stand for the works council next spring. In a year, the union branch at [+ lw_works +] will be ours.
